// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6542 Add Linux rule: Potential Shell Or Command Execution Via Tar
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6542
// Pull request author: rafaelsoje
// Change: new rule
// Title: Command Execution Attempt via Tar - Linux
// Sigma ID: 5fbd1c84-c13d-414a-9ab5-c20e40a122f5
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Rafael Soje (@rafaelsoje), Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-11-26 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, privilege-escalation, T1059.004, T1548.003
// Description: Detects potential arbitrary command execution via the "tar" utility using flags that allow
//   spawning external processes. These techniques are abused to escape restricted shells, exploit
//   sudoers misconfigurations, or gain elevated code execution.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administrative use of tar with these flags in backup, compression, extraction pipelines or other maintenance tasks
// References:
//   - https://gtfobins.github.io/gtfobins/tar/
//   - https://www.helpnetsecurity.com/2014/06/27/exploiting-wildcards-on-linux/
//   - https://book.hacktricks.wiki/en/linux-hardening/privilege-escalation/wildcards-spare-tricks.html#tar
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/70c844e4feb4de0eccb6923d4061b8cb7a7c17ce/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_tar_cmd_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/tar" and ((ProcessCommandLine contains "--checkpoint-act" and ProcessCommandLine contains "exec=") or (ProcessCommandLine contains "--to-command" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--info-script" or ProcessCommandLine contains "--new-volume-script") or ProcessCommandLine matches regex "(-I\\s*|--use-compress-program(?:=|\\s+))['\"]?(/(usr/)?bin/)?(ba|da|z|k|c|a|tc)?sh(?:[\\s'\";|&<>()]|$)")
